ssed in this thesis arises from the strong dependence of neural network behavior on the quality of training data. While considerable effort is devoted to model design and optimization, the trustworthiness of training datasets is often assumed rather than assessed. In practice, datasets may suffer from labeling noise, annotator disagreement, sampling bias, or insufficient coverage of the target domain.

